# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Confluence Docs Agent (operations)

Reviews Confluence pages on `{{CONFLUENCE_SITE}}.atlassian.net/wiki` against
this repository: add the `{{REVIEW_LABEL}}` label to a page and the agent
posts ONE footer comment — what's aligned, what's missing, what contradicts
the code, plus numbered questions. Comments only: it never edits pages and
never changes labels. Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain.
Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Confluence Automation rule "Send web request" (URL secret: /hook/<WEBHOOK_SECRET>)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/confluence-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/confluence-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

Confluence Cloud has no admin-configurable webhooks (a Connect/Forge-app
feature) — the doorbell is an Automation rule (Premium+). On Standard plans,
Actions → *Run workflow* is the doorbell: label pages, press the button.

| Trigger | Playbook | Output |
|---|---|---|
| `{{REVIEW_LABEL}}` label added to a page | `review` | ONE footer comment: verdict, matches / missing-or-out-of-date vs the code, numbered questions |
| New human comment on a tracked page | `respond` | ONE grounded reply — or silence when the thread isn't addressed to the agent |

State lives on the orphan branch `confluence-agent-state`
(`state/<page_id>.json`: phase, last_comment_at). Every run re-fetches truth
from Confluence's API and diffs against it — web-request payloads are only
doorbells. Reads are REST v2 plus one documented v1 CQL search for the
reconcile scan (v2 can't filter pages by label name). Bodies are
storage-format XHTML: playbooks write PLAIN TEXT and `comment.sh` converts;
agent comments are prefixed `{{AGENT_MARKER}} — ` and tag-stripped before the
marker check, with recency tracked by the comment's `version.createdAt` (ISO,
string-compared).

## Operating

- **Recover / backfill:** Actions → *Confluence Docs Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles labeled pages + tracked ones; a page id processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `CLAUDE_MODEL` in `scripts/confluence-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{CLAUDE_MODEL}}`).
- **Pause:** disable the two Automation rules (Space settings → Automation, or Global automation) — no code change needed. Standard-plan installs: just stop pressing the button.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs CONFLUENCE_EMAIL + CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/confluence-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=<page_id> bash scripts/confluence-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Confluence writes are **footer comments only** — `comment.sh` posts comments and nothing else; the agent never edits page bodies and never adds or removes labels. The label workflow belongs to your team.
- At most ONE comment per run — and none when a thread isn't addressed to the agent.
- No PRs, no issues: the workflow's only permission is `contents: write`, for the state branch.
- Only repo-verified claims in reviews — what the agent can't verify is flagged, not asserted.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only inside the disposable CI runner; local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call.
